{
  "$comment": [
    "The public-post quality rule the server applies before a post goes public (getPublicPostQualityError, which src/lib/marketplace-trust.ts re-exports from the shared module below).",
    "The app checks the same rule before step 2 says Ready to publish, so it cannot promise a post the server will refuse.",
    "Both read the rule from one shared module, ugc-mobile/lib/post-publish-policy/post-publish-policy.ts, which lists placeholderTokens, decisivePlaceholderTokens and fillerTokens in code; the database's public.marketplace_text_is_placeholder applies the same rule to recipe posts and is held to these lists by src/__tests__/marketplace-placeholder-sql-migration.test.ts. Each suite holds its side to these cases: src/__tests__/marketplace-trust.test.ts (server) and ugc-mobile/__tests__/post-new-view-model.test.ts (app).",
    "Text is a placeholder when nothing is left once links and everything but letters, marks and digits are removed (punctuation, symbols and emoji of any script); when it holds a decisive token anywhere ('Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet'); when every word is a placeholder token, a filler token or a number and at least one is a placeholder token ('Demo video', 'This is a test post', but not 'Product demo'); or when it is keyboard mash of Latin letters and digits ('ababab'). Letters of any script count as words.",
    "A text post (no media) also needs a body of at least minTextLength characters that is not placeholder text. Private posts are not checked."
  ],
